#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "434e9983-5bd2-56c7-a949-f56896edd2ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbdc50bf-788f-5004-9515-5e6090b8007f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344224} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7a7bd8-7b13-5212-abba-6c05d749b68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344225} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc4cb6a-81c6-52af-bd68-202a6bfd5925" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344226} {:answer/id #uuid "cb3cb9f5-d994-54c0-84dc-0c857f6c4e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344227} {:answer/id #uuid "264bbddf-31a4-5f5f-aea7-a689915fb9d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d7a7bd8-7b13-5212-abba-6c05d749b68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344225} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f652020-5fb4-5f8f-8bff-246b16fa28e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e10680dc-d37c-5d39-bcb4-15462d1936c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161490" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{x+y}(y+2z)\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{x+y}(y+2z)\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[yz+{z}^{2}]_{z=x}^{z=x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y((x+y)-x)+((x+y)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{2}{3}({x}^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}(16-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
